Fix an MPI deadlock in ParFiniteElementSpace::BuildParallelConformingInterpolation
for partitioned nonconforming tetrahedral meshes.

When a tet master face's first-level slave faces are all local and unsplit,
NCMesh::TraverseTriFace skipped emitting the tet edge-face constraints for the
interior edges of the face split. An element of another MPI rank can be
attached to such an interior edge without owning any of the slave faces (an
"edge-only" neighbor). In that case the constraint entry is missing on the
face-owning rank, so ParNCMesh::CalculatePMatrixGroups never adds the
edge-neighbor rank to the P matrix groups of the master face and its edges and
vertices. The owner then never sends those P matrix rows and
BuildParallelConformingInterpolation deadlocks: the edge-neighbor rank spins in
MPI_Iprobe waiting for rows while the remaining ranks enter the collective
HypreParMatrix construction. Triggered by e.g. loading a serial nonconforming
mesh saved by a previous AMR run and distributing it with a METIS partitioning
(SFC-based partitions keep refinement siblings together, which makes the
pattern rare, but arbitrary partitions hit it readily at high rank counts).

Also fix ParNCMesh::MakeSharedList's handling of edge-face constraint slaves:
entity_owner holds GroupIds, not ranks (group 0 is the singleton {MyRank}), and
a locally owned slave edge must mark its (possibly ghost) master face as
locally touched so the master lands in the shared list symmetrically.

